findings.body:
The `boot.js` edit changed `scheduling.init({apiUrl: urlUtils.urlFor('api', {type: 'admin'}, true)})` to `scheduling.init()`. `scheduling/index.js` forwards the argument straight to `post-scheduling/index.js`, whose `init = async (options) => ...` reads `options.apiUrl` at the `new PostScheduler({apiUrl: options.apiUrl, ...})` call. With `options` undefined, that is a `TypeError` inside an async function, so the promise rejects. That rejection propagates through the `Promise.all` in `initServices()`, and the server fails to boot on every environment.

The xmlrpc removal does not need this change, so the fix is to restore the original argument.

::diff{file="ghost/core/core/boot.js" lines="351-372"}

::callout{type="warning"}
This is not caught by the existing unit tests, which removed xmlrpc tests but added none for boot. A boot-level test or a smoke test of `initServices()` would catch it.

::

`slack.listen()` was removed from the `Promise.all` in `boot.js`, but the PR title and description only mention xmlrpc. `slack.js` `listen()` is the only place that registers `slackListener` on `post.published` and `slackTestPing` on `slack.test`. Nothing else in the repo calls it (confirmed with a repo-wide search), so after this change Slack post notifications stop firing, and the `slack.test` event that `api/endpoints/slack.js` emits has no handler. The `const slack = require(...)` at line 319 is now unused too.

If the removal was intentional, it belongs in its own PR with a note saying Slack's legacy integration is retired. Otherwise restore the call.

::diff{file="ghost/core/core/boot.js" lines="351-368"}

::callout{type="warning"}
If it is restored, the `slack` require at line 319 stays in use.

::

`const urlUtils = require('./shared/url-utils');` at line 343 was only used for the `scheduling.init` `apiUrl` argument. That argument was removed, so `urlUtils` is now unused in `initServices()`. Ghost's ESLint config flags unused variables, so this will fail lint. Once the scheduling argument is restored (see the critical finding), this resolves itself.

::diff{file="ghost/core/core/boot.js" lines="343-343"}

::
